  "extraction_notes": [
    "Datasheet identity: ROHM 2SA2029 / 2SA1774EB / 2SA1774 / 2SA1576UB / 2SA1576A / 2SA1037AK, General Purpose Transistor (-50V, -150mA), revision 20150909 - Rev.003. One shared datasheet covers six package variants; the electrical characteristics are common. 2SA1037AK is the SOT-346 (SMT3) variant with PD = 200 mW mounted on a reference footprint; pinout (1) emitter, (2) base, (3) collector.",
    "The supplied PDF contains pages 1 through 6 of the 12-page document. All electrical tables (p. 2) and every electrical characteristic curve (Figs. 1-15, p. 3-6) are present; the missing pages 7-12 carry package drawings and tape information only.",
    "PNP identity and signs are preserved as printed: VCEO, IC, VCE, VBE, VCE(sat), VBE(sat), VCB and VEB are negative. The transition-frequency test condition and Fig. 8 print the emitter current as positive IE, which is retained.",
    "Curves were digitized from a 600 dpi raster. Plot frames and printed gridline positions were located pixel-exactly and used for axis calibration; curve ordinates were taken as the centre of the thick curve stroke at the stated grid abscissae. No interpolation between read-offs was applied.",
    "The 25 degC member of each temperature-family figure was identified by tracing the printed leader lines: Fig. 1 third curve from the left; Fig. 3 third from the top; Fig. 5 third from the top; Fig. 7 second from the top.",
    "Calibration cross-check: the digitized Fig. 8 curve reads 136 MHz at IE = 2 mA versus the table typical fT of 140 MHz at the same bias.",
    "Known datasheet inconsistency: the Fig. 9 typical Cob curve reads about 2.6 pF at VCB = -12 V while the electrical characteristics table states 4.0 pF typical and 5.0 pF maximum at the same bias. The table value is retained in specs.cobo and the curve is reported as digitized.",
    "The electrical characteristics table gives no VBE(sat), VBE(on) or Cib rows, so specs.cibo and all vbe_sat entries are digitized typical-curve values; the table VCE(sat) row (max -500 mV at IC = -50 mA, IB = -5 mA) is kept as a guaranteed maximum and not converted to typical.",
    "hFE 120 to 560 at VCE = -6 V, IC = -1 mA is the full QRS rank span shipped for 2SA1037AKT146R (rank bins Q 120-270, R 180-390, S 270-560). The minimum and maximum are kept as separate gain points because the schema has no range field.",
    "Fig. 2 output-characteristic branches for IB = -100 uA and -500 uA were digitized; the remaining base-current branches and the temperature-family curves other than 25 degC were not extracted.",
    "Fig. 9 axes are logarithmic with the plot frame at VCB/VEB = -0.15 V to -15 V and 1 pF to 20 pF; the Cib curve is only plotted out to about VEB = -2.5 V."
  ],
  "omission_reason": "The strict schema has no fields for V(BR)CBO, V(BR)CEO, V(BR)EBO breakdown rows, ICBO and IEBO cut-off currents, VCBO and VEBO absolute maximum ratings, collector-current and power limits (IC -150 mA, ICP -200 mA, PD 200 mW), thermal ratings (Tj, Tstg), hFE rank classification bins, the non-25 degC temperature-family curves of Figs. 1, 3, 5 and 7, the VCE = -1 V and -2 V gain curves of Fig. 4, the IC/IB = 20 and 50 saturation curves of Fig. 6, or the safe-operating-area curves of Figs. 10-15."
}
